Responsibilities and honesty protected little girl from making even a single bite. She had to deliver all pasties intact. But she could afford herself to have a little rest. Red Hood sat on a stump that was in the shade of a branchy tree. It was much cooler there, than on the Sun burning path. It was caressing warmth and a slight wind blowing that made Red Hood grow languid,  and filled her body with pleasant languor. The girl even closed her eyes.
Suddenly, Wolf came out of nowhere. When Red Hood heard the noise, she flash-like jumped up.